[There’s also a version by Joan Baez (same key but capo'd differently).  Leonard's is easier to play but Joan's is a bit more "soaring".]

FUN FACT:  “Suzanne” is Suzanne Verdal, the girlfriend and later wife of one of Leonard’s friends.  

TIP:  There's a simple lick in the intro/outro and after the chorus that's easy to play.  You hold the (C) form throughout.  Start with a strum of (C) and then pick the covered 4th string <e>, add pinky to the 4th string/3rd fret <f> right under the ring finger, lift off to get back to <e>, and strum (C).  Easy.  (Notes may or may not transpose.)
   

